<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iberians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iberians were the pre-Roman peoples of the eastern and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>, among them the Turdetani, Edetani and Ilergetes. They spoke a non-Indo-European language written in their own scripts, lived in fortified towns and produced sculpture such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lady-of-elche">Lady of Elche</a>. Contact with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthaginians</a> shaped their culture before Roman conquest from the late 3rd century BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iberians.jpg" alt="Iberians" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heparina1985 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lady_of_Elche_at_the_National_Arquaeological_Museum,_Madrid_(Spain).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
